      "imageWidth": 2204,
      "imageHeight": 1632,
      "story": "The East Offering its Riches to Britannia is an oil painting by the Greek artist Spyridon Romas. Born on the island of Corfu, Romas worked in Corfu, Lecce, Livorno, and London. He trained in the Heptanese School and later adopted an English style. In 1770 he settled in London, where he remained for the rest of his life. About twenty-five of his works survive; although he painted a number of portraits during his years in London, The East Offering its Riches to Britannia is his best-known work.",
